  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1254 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nThere will another chance for isolated showers and thunderstorms\nMonday as the weak disturbance dissipates over Central Texas. The\nstrong upper ridge will break down over the northern part of the\ncountry, but continue to control the weather over the southern\nstates. Southeasterly low level flow will keep hot, moist air over\nSouth-Central Texas. There may be some seabreeze convection each\nday Tuesday through Thursday over the Coastal Plains, but chances\nare low. Most of the area will be hot and dry. Temperatures will\nbe steady and above normal through the week.",
